PART 3 — API CONTRACT
Envelope: {"success":true,"data":{...},"error":null} / {"success":false,"data":null,"error":{"message":"..."}} — use the existing kernel_db() response convention if one exists; this is the fallback.
Endpoints (functional list — literal names follow whatever Phase 0 finds): projects (list/get/create/update/archive), project_types (list/get/create/update), stages (list-by-project/create/update/reorder), tasks (list/get/create/update/move/delete), task_dependencies (list/create/delete), custom_fields (list/create/update/delete), custom_field_values (get/upsert), comments (list/create/update/delete), activity_log (list, read-only), docs (list-tree/get/create/update/delete/reorder), labels (list/create/delete), task_labels (attach/detach), attachments (upload/list/delete).
activity_log writes happen automatically inside other actions, never a direct frontend call.
